---
// The Browse triggers. Place them OUTSIDE the reader grid on purpose: a sibling of
// `.reader-layout`, never its third grid child, or they become phantom grid items at desktop
// width. Two buttons, one drawer: the round FAB is the PHONE trigger (CSS-hidden at >=1024px)
// and the labelled "Browse" pill is the DESKTOP trigger (CSS-shown only at >=1024px), so
// exactly one is on screen at any width. Both wear the library glyph (books on a shelf), as does
// the problem page's pill: it says what the drawer is for — the whole shelf, not the one book
// open. A stroked `currentColor` glyph rather than an emoji, so it matches every other control
// and follows the theme. Both share one accessible name, so a screen reader hears the same word
// the pill and the drawer heading show. Either button opens the drawer, which clones
// `.reader-sidebar .reader-sidebar__inner` at click time (islands/reader.ts) and sits OVER the
// page — the desktop sidebar stays as it is. Shared by the server-rendered lesson and the
// private shell.
---

<div class="reader-nav">
  <button class="reader-nav-fab" aria-label="Browse — every lesson in this book" aria-expanded="false" type="button">
    <svg
      class="reader-nav-fab__ic"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      stroke-width="2"
      stroke-linecap="round"
      stroke-linejoin="round"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      <path d="m16 6 4 14 M12 6v14 M8 8v12 M4 4v16" />
    </svg>
  </button>
  <button class="reader-contents-pill" aria-label="Browse — every lesson in this book" aria-expanded="false" type="button">
    <svg
      class="reader-contents-pill__ic"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      stroke-width="2"
      stroke-linecap="round"
      stroke-linejoin="round"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      <path d="m16 6 4 14 M12 6v14 M8 8v12 M4 4v16" />
    </svg>
    <span>Browse</span>
  </button>
</div>
